    {
      "name": "Authentification",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Authentification (login)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Statut 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Un accessToken est retourne\", function () {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    // Le token est automatiquement enregistre pour les requetes suivantes",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", body.accessToken);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"awa.traore.k93x\",\n  \"password\": \"Xk92mQ1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth"]
            },
            "description": "Authentifie un utilisateur et retourne un token JWT.\n\nAuthentification requise : Non\n\nContent-Type : application/json\n\nCorps de la requete (JSON) :\n{\n  \"username\": \"string (accepte le username OU l'email)\",\n  \"password\": \"string\"\n}\n\nFormat de reponse (200) :\n{\n  \"accessToken\": \"string (JWT)\"\n}\n\nLe token JWT contient : l'identifiant (sub), l'email, le username et le role de l'utilisateur.\nA utiliser ensuite dans l'en-tete : Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>\n\nErreurs possibles :\n- 400 : corps de requete invalide (champs manquants)\n- 401 : username/email ou mot de passe incorrect"
          },
